title: Start
---
<<declare $talked_to_wife = false>>
<<declare $read_pennant = false>>
<<declare $has_ring = false>>
<<declare $has_key = false>>

<<if $has_key>>
    <<jump Wife_Done>>
<<elseif $has_ring>>
    <<jump Wife_RingFound>>
<<elseif $talked_to_wife>>
    <<jump Wife_Reminder>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Wife_Intro>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Wife_Intro
---
Wife: I wonder where my dear husband pookie bear Oski is...
Goober: Ummmm... okay... do you happen to have a key?
Wife: O-oh hi there! I actually picked up an old key on campus the other day.
Wife: I won't just give it to you though. I need your help.
Wife: MY WEDDING RING HAS GONE MISSING!!!
Wife: Help me find my wedding ring and I'll give you the key, deal? Unless you have, you know, some other information about my husband…
<<set $talked_to_wife to true>>
-> Girl what. I'll find your wedding ring I guess.
-> Oski won't like that you lost your ring… <<if $read_pennant>>
    <<jump Wife_Situation>>
===

title: Wife_Situation
---
Wife: Waaaaaittt... what? How do you know the name of my dear husband pookie bear?
-> Your husband's a stalker. Leave him now.
    Wife: Huh, how'd you know?
    Goober: He wrote "I'm in your walls" on your Cal pennant! That's so weird!
    Wife: Awww he wrote that? How sweet of him! He loves me so much.
    Goober: EXCUSE ME?
    Wife: WHAT! Are you judging me?! Get out of my room, loser!
-> Oski's dead. I had a vision where I saw his ghost.
    Wife: OSKI!? MY BEAUTIFUL HANDSOME TALL SMART STRONG NONCHALANT CUTIE POOKIE BEAR OSKI?
    Goober: Yes. Look, his ghost left this message on your Cal pennant. "I'm in your walls." He's definitely a ghost, girl.
    Wife: That's not enough evidence. He could have written it alive!
    Goober: Uhm actually, no he couldn't, because why else would he write this sentence? To be in your walls, one must not have a physical body. To not have a physical body, one must be air, aka dead. He's watching over you in the spirit realm!!! Just trust me bro.
    Wife: Ohh... I see... that makes sense. *sniff* So what do I do now? I'm gonna cry.
    Goober: Don't cry! Look, Oski's dead, which means you can get a beautifuller, handsomer, taller, smarter, stronger, nonchalant-er husband okay?
    Wife: *sniff* Okay...
    Goober: And you can interview for 20 consulting clubs to numb the pain, okay?
    Wife: *sniff sniff sniff* Okay...
    Goober: Aaaand about that ring—you don't need it anymore, okay?
    Wife: *hiccup* You're right... take the key and get out of my sight... *sniff sniff* I need some alone time…
    <<set $has_key to true>>
===

title: Wife_Reminder
---
Wife: Did you find my wedding ring yet?
-> Still looking.
-> Oski won't like that you lost your ring… <<if $read_pennant>>
    <<jump Wife_Situation>>
===

title: Wife_RingFound
---
Wife: Oh! You actually found my beautiful wedding ring! Thank you so much!
Wife: Here’s the key. I must continue looking for my husband now.
<<set $has_key to true>>
===

title: Wife_Done
---
// Placeholder: shown if you talk to her after getting the key
Wife: Please... I need some alone time.
===

title: Wife_Pennant
---
Player: I think someone wrote something on this Cal pennant...
Player: "I'm in your walls... - Oski"
<<set $read_pennant to true>>
===

title: Toilet_Intro
---
<<declare $toilet_clicks = 0>>
Player: It's a toilet. I see something shiny is stuck inside the drain...
Player: Maybe if I flush it enough times it'll come loose.
===

title: Toilet_Progress
---
<<if $toilet_clicks >= 499>>
    Player: I can feel it. One more flush. ONE MORE.
<<elseif $toilet_clicks >= 400>>
    Player: My wrist hurts. Why am I doing this for a ring.
<<elseif $toilet_clicks >= 250>>
    Player: Halfway there... I think it moved a little?
<<elseif $toilet_clicks >= 100>>
    Player: 100 flushes. The water bill is going to be so high
<<else>>
    Player: *flush*
<<endif>>
===

title: Toilet_Ring
---
Player: ...!!! Something popped out!
Player: It's a wedding ring. Gross. But it has a HUGE diamond.
<<set $has_ring to true>>
===

title: Toilet_Done
---
Player: I am never touching a toilet again.
===
